<title>GERMANY: Varta says loss situation improved.</title>
<headline>Varta says loss situation improved.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German battery maker Varta AG said on Thursday its sales fell two percent in the first half of 1996 but its loss situation had improved.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that its results improved from a loss of 24 million marks to a figure of eight million but it did not say if this was a loss or profit.</p>
<p>No one was immediately available at the company for comment.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
